\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Ends Weaker on Change in S&P Ratings View\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2013\par 22:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real lost ground against the dollar to end weaker in a volatile session Friday as investors took a defensive stance following a downward revision of \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  ratings outlook for local government assets.\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRL2.1328 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.1205 to the dollar Thursday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  took a steep dive at the outset of trading, moving to around BRL2.15 to the dollar, after S&P late Thursday lowered its outlook for Brazilian government securities to negative from stable. In making the revision, the agency cited adverse effects of weak growth and an eroding fiscal stance in the country.\par \par \uc2 The real, however, changed direction in intraday trading to strengthen, amid reports mobile telecom operator Claro made a $300 million transaction in the local market. Exporters also reportedly took advantage of the spike to cash in dollars for local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real weakened yet again later in the session when Finance Minister Guido Mantega moved to dispel rumors about new measures to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide during an interview with the Estado news agency. Mr. Mantega, however, said the government would stay attentive to excessive volatility, suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may still be active with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 "There is always some volatility, because we have a floating exchange rate," he said.\par \par \uc2 Market participants, however, weren't entirely convinced that the government was done tinkering with capital control policies and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially considering the possible impacts of the latest S&P decision.\par \par \uc2 "It's likely there'll be some intense discussions between finance and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials in the coming days to determine what direction they'll take policy from here," said Joao Paulo Correa, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at the Correparti brokerage in Curitiba.\par \par \uc2 Brazil this week eliminated its 6% IOF financial transactions tax on incoming fixed income investments, and market players believe it might make a similar move for a tax on derivatives \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A move to boost inflows, they note, could help strengthen the real further, and ease the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's need to continue raising interest rates this year as part of its fight against accelerated local inflation that has lingered near the 6.5% upper limit of the country's inflation-targeting band.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 07-06-13 2013GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130607e967000oe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
