\par\par \b \uc2 Barron's Blog:Brazil Ends Tax on Foreign Investors, Stocks Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2013\par 21:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on Barron's Online's Emerging Markets Daily at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Ben Levisohn\par \par \uc2 Foreigners can invest freely in Brazil again. The question now is if they'll want to.\par \par \uc2 Late yesterday, Brazil removed a tax on foreign investors that had been put in place to prevent a rush of short-term cash into that nation's financial markets. The Wall Street Journal has the details:\par \par \uc2 With Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening, Finance Minister Guido Mantega Tuesday lifted a years-old tax on foreign bond buyers and other overseas investors...The tax was cut to zero from 6% because of changes in the global financial landscape, he said.\par \par \uc2 Talking to reporters after a meeting with President Dilma Rousseff, Mr. Mantega said the conditions that made his ministry levy the tax a couple of years ago are no longer in place. "We had a flood of capital," he said, referring to inflows of dollars in emerging markets from investors seeking better returns.\par \par \uc2 Marketfield's Micheal Shaoul ponders the timing:\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2 ' Guilherme Loureiro and Marcelo Salomon think the move could be counterproductive:\par \par \uc2 We welcome the move as it reduces the distortions created by penalizing flows into Brazil and believe that in the short run the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will test again the 2.05 level against the USD. Moreover, the very attractive carry that Brazil offers could favor bull flattening of the curve. However, we are also of the view that zeroing the IOF tax eliminates an important barrier that prevented foreign investors from liquidating local rates positions (as they would have had to pay tax again to push money into Brazil). And the elimination of this barrier should, in fact, increase the volatility of USD/BRL, especially in moments of stress in global capital markets. While the decision to cut the IOF tax helps attract foreign flows, it also will demand more \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the BCB to dampen excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 UPDATE: \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been buoyed by the news, gaining as much as 0.4% against the dollar, but is now roughly unchanged against the greenback at 3:15pm. It's dropped more than 5% during the past month even as \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates. The iShares MSCI Brazil Capped Index ETF ( EWZ) had been up 0.7% to $51.49 , but is now down 1.8% at %50.20, as Vale ( VALE) has fallen 2.9% to $14.58 and \uc2 GOL Linhas Aereas Inteligentes\uc2  ( GOL) has dipped 2.8% to $4.21, after being up 3% earlier today. The \uc2 iShares MSCI Emerging Markets Index ETF\uc2  ( EEM) has dropped 1.4% to $41.26. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  For continuously updated news from Barron's, see Barrons.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://barrons.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://barrons.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 05, 2013 15:33 ET (19:33 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130605e965004tz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
