\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Falls After Official Says Weakening 'Inevitable'\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2013\par 21:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil real exits active trading at BRL2.1348/dollar\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director says weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "inevitable"\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen less frequent in future\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  By Paulo Winterstein \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's real weakened Tuesday after the director of monetary policy for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decline against the U.S. dollar was "inevitable," leading many traders to see room for a further drop in value.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.1348 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, after closing on Monday at BRL2.1253 per dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real opened stronger after statistics institute IBGE said output at Brazil's mines and factories rose considerably more than economists had expected in April. Industrial production rose 1.8% in April from March, more than the 1% month-on-month increase expected by economists polled by Brazil's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agencia Estado\f28 \uc2 \f2  news service.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the real weakened rapidly after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aldo Mendes\f28 \uc2 \f2 , monetary policy director at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are all weakening against the dollar, and so the real's weakness is inevitable. "There's nothing I can do," he said about the real's weakness.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market was fine until these comments from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aldo Mendes\f28 \uc2 \f2 ," said Jose Carlos Amado, a fixed-income trader at the Renascenca brokerage in Sao Paulo. "He basically said that they're going to leave the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alone since it's a general tendency."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Whereas in the past the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in markets to contain sudden losses to the real, Tuesday's comments signaled that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could stay on the sidelines in the near future.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We only react when we aren't together with the others," Mr. Mendes said. "If we're moving in step with the other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the world, there's no reason to enter the market."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, the real shied away from the mark of BRL2.15 per dollar, a level it last breached in 2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last week, the real approached BRL2.15, but traders were surprised by a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meant to strengthen the real.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last Wednesday reported weaker-than-expected growth in the first quarter, and that was quickly followed by a bigger-than-expected increase in the country's benchmark Selic interest rate. Concerned about faltering growth, investors on Friday sold off the real in droves. After the real traded as weak as BRL2.1443 per dollar, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $877 million of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap contracts--normally used to strengthen the real--and temporarily halted the decline.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said that such auctions are uncommon on the last day of the month, when exchange rates for futures contracts are settled. As such, the auction signaled that policy makers are still reluctant to let the real weaken too quickly against the dollar, even though such weakness could help a recovery in Brazilian exports of manufactured goods. For the past six months, the government has tended to step in whenever the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strayed too far from a range of BRL1.95 to BRL2.05 per dollar, but in recent weeks the government has let the real slide a bit more.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com [ 04-06-13 1930GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130604e964000na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
