\par\par \b \uc2 Weaker real to have limited impact on Brazil inflation-Tombini\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2013\par 00:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief says weaker real due to global factors\par \par \uc2 * Bank ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt "excessive volatility"\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, June 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief on Sunday said  the recent weakening of the local real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2    should have "limited" impact on inflation, but that the bank is ready to step in if needed to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.\par \par \uc2 The real ended at 2.1412 per dollar on Friday, its weakest level since May 2009, because of increased global risk aversion on concerns of a possible withdrawal of U.S. stimulus measures and speculation by local investors about policymakers' tolerance to a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This is a global movement of the U.S. dollar not something peculiar to Brazil," \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  said in comments provided by the bank's press office during a media briefing in Istanbul, Turkey. "Provided that the exchange rate regime is flexible as it is the case in Brazil the pass through should be limited."\par \par \uc2 Tombini was participating in a seminar organized by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 The sharp weakening of the real could push up the value of imported goods, stoking already high inflation in the South American nation that only two decades ago was suffering with  hyperinflation.\par \par \uc2 To fight inflation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday surprised investors by speeding up the pace of its monetary tightening cycle with a 50-basis-points rate hike.\par \par \uc2 In theory, that rate hike should ease the pressure on the real as it increases the appeal of Brazilian fixed-income assets that lures more U.S. dollars into the local market.\par \par \uc2 However, neither the rate increase nor a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Friday was able to prop up the real.\par \par \uc2 Tombini reiterated that the bank could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to stem "excessive volatility" in the real via the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot and future market as well as by providing dollar trade lines to exporters.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered trade lines to Brazilian exporters in 2008 when external financing dried up during the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 In the 12 months to mid-May, inflation slowed to 6.46  percent, just slightly below the official target range ceiling of 6.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/INFLATION | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | C | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130602e962000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
