\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Brazil real hits 4-year low, interest-rate futures rally\b0\par\par\uc2 766 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2013\par 14:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real slumps on risk aversion, cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Selic increase by 50 bps sends rate futures rallying\par \par \uc2 * Markets see turning point in fight against inflation\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, May 31 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real closed at a four-year low on Friday despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while interest-rate futures rallied after policymakers raised the benchmark Selic rate by more than investors expected.\par \par \uc2 The real ended at 2.1412 per dollar, its weakest level since May 2009, even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up its campaign against inflation, a move that potentially increases the appeal of Brazilian fixed-income assets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses were triggered by a combination of global risk aversion related to a possible withdrawal of U.S. stimulus measures and speculation by local investors about policymakers' tolerance to a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Not even a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier on Friday was able to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank sold \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivative contracts designed to strengthen the real, but the auction only temporarily cushioned the real's decline.\par \par \uc2 A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a headache for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it could add to inflation by making imported goods more expensive. A sharp depreciation of the real could also increase \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks to companies exposed to exchange rate fluctuations.\par \par \uc2 For now, however, government officials might just be giving some time for investors to digest a series of market developments domestically and abroad.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Reuters, a government source said policymakers "have to wait and see what is going to happen" to the U.S. bond-buying program, which for years has provided a steady source of dollars seeking higher returns in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 A higher-than-expected increase in Brazil's Selic rate also "tends to mitigate" the depreciation of the real, the source said.\par \par \uc2 "It's still early to say at which level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the real to trade, especially after (finance minister Guido) Mantega said a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is good for exporters, which caused all that speculation," said Glauber Romano, a trader with Intercam brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already signaling it won't allow the real to weaken much further," Romano added.\par \par \uc2 INTEREST-RATE FUTURES RALLY\par \par \uc2 Brazilian interest-rate futures rallied, however, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to speed up the pace of monetary tightening was seen as a turning point in the bank's fight against inflation.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday evening lifted the Selic by 50 basis points to 8.0 percent in a unanimous decision announced hours before the start of a national holiday on Thursday, which shut financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the announcement of the decision, many economists and investors had bet policymakers would keep raising borrowing costs at a more modest pace as economic activity falters.\par \par \uc2 "The acceleration in the rate hike pace and a unanimous decision shows a surprising resolve of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to renew focus on inflation," Siobhan Morden, head of Latin America strategy at \uc2 Jefferies and Co\uc2 , wrote in a research note.\par \par \uc2 While yields paid on short-dated interest rate contracts are surely going to rally, the real question is whether investors will continue to ask for more inflation premium in the longer-dated contracts, Morden said.\par \par \uc2 So far on Friday, the shape of Brazil's domestic yield curve remained little changed, with the most liquid contracts rising in block.\par \par \uc2 Interest-rate contracts maturing in January 2014, one of the most traded, jumped 36 basis points to 8.42. Longer-dated contracts expiring in January 2017 also rose 36 basis points, to 9.74 percent.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's yield curve now prices in at least another Selic hike of 50 basis points in July, according to Reuters' calculations. Some analysts said an additional and final rate hike of 25 or 50 basis points could also be on tap.\par \par \uc2 That is a sign that investors expect policymakers to aggressively fight inflation even after key GDP data on Wednesday showed Brazil's economy expanded 0.6 percent in the first quarter, less than the 0.9 percent forecast by economists.\par \par \uc2 Responding to concerns rate hikes could hurt growth, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  on Thursday said in a TV interview the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move will increase investors' "confidence in the pillars of the Brazilian economy," helping in the economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-MARKETS/POSTCOPOM  (UPDATE 3) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130531e95v000mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
