\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2 , Stocks Fall on Lower-Than-Expected Economic Growth\b0\par\par\uc2 779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2013\par 23:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil's real ended active trading at the BRL2.10 to the dollar level\par \par \uc2 --The Ibovespa index fell 2.5% to 54634 points\par \par \uc2 --Brazil's first-quarter GDP grew 1.9% from a year earlier, below expectations\par \par \uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks finished lower Wednesday on disappointing first-quarter economic data, which lead economists to cut estimates for the full year.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real, now trading at its lowest levels since December 2012, exited active trading at BRL2.1084 to the dollar, after closing Tuesday at BRL2.0718 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Most stocks in the Ibovespa index also finished lower. The index closed down 2.5% at 54634 points.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's gross domestic product grew 1.9% in the first quarter from a year earlier, the Brazilian Institute of Geography and Statistics, or IBGE, said. The figure was below economists' estimates for 2.38% expansion.\par \par \uc2 The data signal that the Brazilian economy will be stuck in a range below 3% for longer-than-expected period, according to Tony Volpon at Nomura Securities, who cut his estimates for 2013 growth to 2.5% from 3.4%.\par \par \uc2 Banco Fibra\uc2  also revised down its growth projections for the year, to 2.4% from 2.8%. "In terms of demand, GDP's growth in the first quarter of 2013 has slowed in all its components compared to the previous quarter, with the exception of investments, which went up from 1.3% in the fourth quarter of 2012 to 4.6% in the first quarter of 2013," the bank said in a note to the market.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Guido Mantega admitted in a press conference Wednesday that the latest official growth estimate of 3.5% in 2013 would now need to be revised. He also said the recent weakening of the Brazilian real reflects investors' expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve will soon reverse some of its monetary easing. However, the minister added, the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't a concern for the government at the moment as it will help Brazil's trade balance.\par \par \uc2 "Whenever Mr. Mantega talks, he brings volatility to the markets," said Reginaldo Galhardo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at brokerage Treviso, adding the ministers estimates constantly have proven wrong.\par \par \uc2 The real is "having a bad hair day" trading thru BRL2.10 after the Finance Minister talked down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nomura Securities' Aloisio Teles said in a note to the market mid-afternoon. "Corporates are starting to get uneasy and if authorities do not do anything in line with past actions we can easily see an uncontrolled move," he added.\par \par \uc2 Traders have been on a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch, expecting \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might act at any time to shore up the real. Some said it didn't happen Wednesday because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to postpone an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a calmer day.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will decide later Wednesday if the key interest rate should be raised as part of its efforts to control inflation. Economists expect a rate hike but are divided over whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise rates by 0.25% percentage point or 0.50 percentage points. The base Selic rate currently stands at 7.50% per year.\par \par \uc2 "I believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will wait till Friday, following a holiday this Thursday, to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive down the dollar," said Luiz Carlos Baldan, a director at local brokerage Fourtrade.\par \par \uc2 In the Brazilian stock exchange, most shares finished in the red. The Ibovespa fall was led by oil firm \uc2 OGX Petroleo e Gas\uc2  Participacoes, controlled by billionaire Eike Batista. The company's shares fell 8.43% to BRL1.52.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian blue ships also finished lower. Mining behemoth Vale shares fell 0.74% to BRL29.55. Shares of government-run energy firm \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  fell 0.85% to BRL19.90.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, shares of Brazilian real-estate developer Gafisa had the biggest gains in the index on reports the company could be close to selling its Alphaville Urbanismo unit. Shares finished 3.02% up at BRL4.10.\par \par \uc2 Gafisa has received offers from bidders including Equity International, controlled by magnate Sam Zell, and U.S. investment advisory firm Blackstone and Patria Investments, a Brazilian firm, according to a source. Offers have ranged from around BRL1.5 billion to around BRL2 billion, and Blackstone and Patria, which are bidding together, seem to be ahead, the person added.\par \par \uc2 Gafisa, Equity International and Blackstone declined to comment. Spokespeople at Patria weren't immediately available for comments.\par \par \uc2 Write to Luciana Magalhaes at luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 29, 2013 17:32 ET (21:32 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130529e95t005xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
