\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Brazil's Mantega: 1Q GDP Shows Strong Economic Growth\b0\par\par\uc2 850 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2013\par 16:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:39 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Global Economy Conditions Are Adverse\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:39 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Finance Minister Guido Mantega Speaks At Press Conference\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:40 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Finance Minister Discusses 1Q GDP Result\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:43 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Finally, Investment is Reacting to Stimulus\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:46 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Government Won't Offer New Stimulus Measures\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:47 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Consumer Must Recover From Dynamism of Investments\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:47 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Some Stimulus Has Already Been Withdrawn\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:47 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Consumption Mustn't be Driver of Growth\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:49 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Government Will Ensure Electric Power Rates Don't Rise\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:52 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Weakening A Response to US Federal Reserve\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:52 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Weakening 'Isn't A Concern For Us'\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:52 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Mantega: No Government \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:52 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Market Forces Are Driving \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:53 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Helps With Trade Balance\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:53 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Started 2013 In Better Position Than In 2012\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:54 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Can Achieve 'Satisfactory' Growth This Year\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:55 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Will Review 3.5% GDP Forecast For 2013\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:56 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Second Quarter Economic Data Are 'Very Good'\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 10:59 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Growth Forecast Will Be Revised Downwards\par \par \uc2 29 May 2013 11:54 EDT DJ  Brazil's Mantega Strikes Sober Tone on 2013 Growth Outlook\par \par \uc2 By Matthew Cowley\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Known for his eternal optimism, Brazil's Finance Minister struck a more sober tone on Wednesday, acknowledging that economic growth would likely fall short of the government's latest forecast following weaker-than-expected first-quarter growth.\par \par \uc2 The latest official forecast for growth this year is 3.5%, and Guido Mantega said that would have to be revised following the first-quarter result.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's gross domestic product grew 0.6% in the first quarter compared with the fourth quarter of 2012, below the 0.9% that had been expected. The disappointing number has already led some private-sector economists to lower their forecast for this year: \uc2 Banco Fibra\uc2  cut its forecast to 2.4% for the year, from 2.8% previously.\par \par \uc2 "Our preliminary estimates for GDP growth in the next few quarters aren't at all cheering," says Banco Fibra chief economist Cristiano Oliveira in a note. "There are constraints on the supply side that will impact Brazilian growth in this period. The rate for potential GDP growth has shown a significant and worrying deceleration in the last quarters."\par \par \uc2 Weaker growth may feed into the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on interest rates due later Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began raising its key interest rate, the Selic, at its last meeting, amid worryingly high inflation.\par \par \uc2 After the data was released, investors pared back some of their bets on Wednesday's decision, and now expect an increase of 0.25 percentage point, which would lift the rate to 7.75% per year, from the previous expectation of 0.50 percentage point.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Mantega said he believes the first quarter was evidence of "strong" economic growth, despite adverse international scenario, and one in which investment in particular showed signs of recovery. The economy started the year in better shape than it started 2012, and "satisfactory" growth can be achieved this year, he said.\par \par \uc2 "Finally investment is reacting to the stimulus that the government has been providing in recent years," Mr. Mantega said.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, there was a change in tone, as the minister said that consumption would no longer be the main driver of economic growth. As such, the government won't offer any new stimulus measures, he said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the minister said that the government will ensure that electric power rates don't rise. Congress may block a decree signed earlier this year by Brazil's President Dilma Rousseff earlier this year that lowered electric power rates.\par \par \uc2 The recent weakening of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to the fact that investors are starting to bet the U.S. Federal Reserve will withdraw some of its monetary easing, Mr. Mantega said. The weaker Brazilian real isn't a concern, as it will help the country's trade balance, the minister said.\par \par \uc2 The minister said the government isn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and market forces are driving the move.\par \par \uc2 Write to Matthew Cowley at matthew.cowley@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 29, 2013 11:54 ET (15:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130529e95t003l2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
