\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  dips as U.S. data stokes fear of Fed pullback\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2013\par 17:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, May 28 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged lower on Tuesday after a surprising jump in U.S. consumer confidence supported the case for an early withdrawal of U.S. stimulus measures, a move that could reduce investors' appetite for high-yielding assets. Brazil's real weakened past 2.06 per dollar for the first time since late December as data showed U.S. consumer confidence strengthened in May to the highest level in more than five years. Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have posted losses over the past two weeks on concerns that the U.S. Federal Reserve may soon cut back on stimulus measures that have provided a steady source of dollars seeking higher returns in emerging markets. * The Brazilian real lost half a percentage point to 2.0668 per dollar, its weakest intraday level since Dec. 26.\par \par \uc2  * Investors in the real feared \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent a sharper \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation that could add to inflation pressures, but analysts said an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to come before policymakers decide on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's base interest rate on Wednesday. * Jaime Ferreira, a manager at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk of Intercam brokerage in Sao Paulo, said of the outlook for the real: "If we see a large interest rate hike tomorrow, that will result in a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it improves the outlook for capital inflows." * Brazil's domestic yield curve mostly prices in a 50-basis-point hike in the country's Selic rate, which currently stands at 7.50 percent. But many economists estimate the rate will go up by a more modest 25 basis points, according to a Reuters poll. * Mexico's peso dropped 0.4 percent to 12.5120 per dollar, nearing a more than two-month low it hit last week. * Chile's peso dipped 0.1 percent to 490.50 per dollar, on track to close at its weakest level in over 10 months, with traders citing continued demand for dollars in the local market. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prices at 1545 GMT:\par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                      change   change\par                             Latest           \par  Brazil real                2.0668    -0.54    -1.30\par                                              \par  Mexico peso               12.5120    -0.40     2.81\par                                              \par  Chile peso               490.5000    -0.10    -2.41\par                                              \par  Colombia peso           1896.3000    -0.91    -6.87\par                                              \par  Peru sol                   2.6780     0.00    -4.74\par                                              \par  Argentina peso             5.2700    -0.05    -6.78\par  Argentina peso             8.8300     1.13   -23.22\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130531e95s000yf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
