\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CHAT:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real's weakness raises specter of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 136 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2013\par 19:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real is weakening sharply, breaking through the BRL2.07-per-dollar mark and raising the specter of action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say. Real now trades at its weakest level since late December, with the US dollar reaching as high as BRL2.0753. "We enter into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  territory above BRL2.07," warns one trader. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained on sidelines since selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps March 27, when the real weakened to nearly BRL2.03. Some traders think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be willing to let real weaken to BRL2.08, a level seen supporting local exporters and manufacturers, but not adding to inflationary pressures. (jeff.fick@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 28, 2013 13:09 ET (17:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130528e95s00440\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
