\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Strengthens vs Dollar on Fed Continuity, Tombini Speech\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Winterstein   \par \uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2013\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's real strengthened slightly Tuesday after some members of the U.S. Federal Reserve signaled their support for continuing an asset-purchase program, while Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  reiterated his mission to combat inflation ahead of next week's monetary policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 The real reversed weakness from earlier in the day and exited active trading at 2.0354 per dollar, slightly stronger than the previous day's close at BRL2.0365 per dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 In a Tuesday speech, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis President \uc2 James Bullard\uc2  voiced his support for continuing the so-called quantitative-easing program, which injects more dollars into markets. The Fed's \uc2 William Dudley\uc2 , meanwhile, said that while bond-buying could slow, it remains possible the Fed may in fact have to increase its purchases if the economy needs support.\par \par \uc2 That alleviated concern the Fed would stop its bond-buying program, which has helped keep global markets flush with dollars and the greenback relatively weak against global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Those concerns earlier in the day had led the dollar to strengthen against the real.\par \par \uc2 "Here and across the world we've seen \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  be very volatile on the question of liquidity," said Anderson Rodrigues, a fixed-income manager at Daycoval Asset Management. "While we have one group at the Fed defending the elimination of the stimulus, others are saying that unemployment is too high and inflation too low."\par \par \uc2 That, of course, contrasts with the situation in Brazil, where unemployment is at record lows, further pressuring inflation that has remained stubbornly close to the upper limit of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation target.\par \par \uc2 In a speech Tuesday afternoon, Mr. Tombini repeated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will act in a "timely manner" to control inflation, stoking debate about whether the next interest-rate increase will be a half-percentage point or a quarter point.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates for the first time in almost two years last month as consumer prices climbed faster than the 6.5% upper limit of the bank's inflation target. With inflation expectations remaining high--a weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey of economists published Monday showed estimates for inflation at 5.8% for this year and next--the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to raise the rate to 8.25% by year-end.\par \par \uc2 "If we had a more efficient market, that increase in rates would have a stronger effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but since the market here is inefficient that doesn't pass through," Mr. Rodrigues said.\par \par \uc2 Higher rates at home than abroad often attract overseas investors to borrow abroad and buy Brazilian securities. However, the Brazilian government has put in place some barriers to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening too quickly, discouraging some investors from coming to \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped corral the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into an informal trading band for the past several weeks.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the real almost weakened to BRL2.05, a level which usually has prompted some reaction from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . According to Mr. Rodrigues, the market will continue testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  range-bound.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com [ 21-05-13 2029GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130521e95l000qs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
