\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Vale CEO sees trouble in Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 , rising wages\b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2013\par 20:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds executive quote, background)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, May 7 (Reuters) - Brazilian industries are struggling with a less competitive exchange rate and fast wage growth, the chief executive of giant mining company \uc2 Vale SA\par \par \uc2 said on Tuesday, underscoring issues that have hampered corporate earnings.\par \par \uc2 "Having the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of place and the significant salary increases are the cost of the great advance in Brazilians' incomes. Everything has its counterpart," Vale CEO \uc2 Murilo Ferreira\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 His remarks at a gathering of executives and government officials sponsored by a Brazilian magazine underscored eroding corporate profitability in Brazil amid the fastest cost inflation and wage growth in years.\par \par \uc2 More than 40 percent of Brazilian companies polled by Thomson Reuters reported lower profit margins in the first quarter, mainly due to rising labor costs and operating expenses.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have helped to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, by about 25 percent in two years, but it remains about 50 percent stronger than it was a decade ago.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Guillermo Parra-Bernal and Gustavo Bonato; Editing by Gerald E. McCormick and Jeffrey Benkoe)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/COSTS (UPDATE 1) | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | O | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD | PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130507e957000z8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2