\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Little Changed Ahead of Trade Figures\b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2013\par 14:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jeffrey T. Lewis\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's real opened little changed against the dollar Monday ahead of monthly trade figures for March.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The real was trading at about BRL2.0199 Monday morning, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, from BRL2.02020 Friday.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's trade ministry will report figures on the trade balance for March on Monday afternoon. In February, the country had a deficit of $1.28 billion, and markets expect a surplus of $150 million for last month, according to Darwin Dib, an economist at CM Capital Markets in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Traders are keeping an eye on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, after the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on March 27, via a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap auction, when the real weakened in morning trading to nearly BRL2.03 versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 As long as the real stays away from the level, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should remain out of the market, said Luiz Carlos Baldan, director of the Fourtrade brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "If the real stays around current levels, we don't expect them to get in," he said of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazilian economists and analysts increased their forecasts for the country's inflation rate for the next year, for the third consecutive week, while they kept unchanged their outlook for this year, according to a weekly \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey released Monday.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said they now expect inflation for the end of 2014 to be 5.68%, up from last week's 5.60%. For the end of 2013, economists maintained their view for inflation at 5.71%.\par \par \uc2 --Rogerio Jelmayer in Sao Paulo contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Jeffrey T. Lewis\uc2  at jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com. [ 01-04-13 1253GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130401e941000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
