\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Strengthens on  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 20:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real exits active trading at BRL2.0066 to the dollar, versus BRL2.0137 the previous day\par \par \uc2 --Real strengthens after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells swap contracts\par \par \uc2 --Trading range likely to remain at BRL2.00-BRL2.03 versus the dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Tom Murphy \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real ended active trading Wednesday stronger against the U.S. dollar following a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  auction of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap contracts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real ended active trading at BRL2.0066 to the dollar, stronger against the Tuesday close of BRL2.0137, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, via the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -swap auction, after the real weakened in morning trading to nearly BRL2.03 versus the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The swap auction allows investors to exchange contracts linked to domestic interest rates for paper indexed to the U.S. dollar. The auction tends to weaken the dollar, and strengthen the real, by putting more dollar-hedged contracts in investors' hands. Wednesday's auction resulted in the sale of nearly $1 billion in swaps.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The auction was in line with the idea that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't like a lot of volatility in daily trading," said Mauricio Gaioti, a trader at Sao Paulo's Ouro Minas brokerage. Mr. Gaioti said it was likely the real will trade in a fairly narrow range during the next few days between BRL2.00 and BRL2.03 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Longer term, however, the real could see some slippage against the dollar because of poor investment inflows. "We could soon see a range of BRL2.01 to BRL2.05 to the dollar," Mr. Gaioti said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global investors have become highly risk-averse in light of new debt and political problems in Europe.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The news from Europe is all bad and that is weighing on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, stocks and commodities," said Marcos Morais, a trader at Sao Paulo brokerage Intercam.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tiny Cyprus faces continued problems as its government wrestles with a complex banking and debt crisis, while Italian political parties have come to an impasse on the formation of a new government. Both countries are weighed down heavily by debts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More broadly, signs from Europe on Wednesday were negative regarding economic recovery. The region's economic sentiment index fell in March to 90.0 points from 91.1 points in February, the first decline since October. It was an apparent indication that consumer and business confidence are feeling the pressure from continued debt problems.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European worries led to a decline in the euro against the U.S. dollar and undermined prices of stocks and commodities world-wide. Lower commodities prices hurt Brazil, in particular, since Brazil is a major commodities exporter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Tom Murphy at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 27-03-13 1953GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130327e93r000vi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
