\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Little Changed Versus Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 13:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--Brazil's real opened little changed against the dollar Tuesday as investors remained cautious about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite headwinds in global markets.\par \par \uc2 Around 8:50 EDT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted trading at BRL2.0118 to the dollar, slightly stronger against Monday's close of BRL2.0120.\par \par \uc2 Notwithstanding the gain, Brazil's real remains around its weakest levels versus the dollar since late January, when the exchange rate broke below BRL2.0 after several months of trading above that mark.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the catalyst back then, through a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at strengthening the real to control rising inflation, analysts said. After trading mostly between BRL1.95 and BRL2.0, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened beyond that range last week amid financial troubles in Cyprus.\par \par \uc2 Though Cyprus appears to have avoided becoming the first country to exit the euro zone, the terms of its 10-billion-euro bailout package worried investors and precluded a global relief rally. The country implemented capital controls to avoid a run on its banks and imposed losses on large depositors, setting a worrisome precedent in the euro-zone debt fiasco.\par \par \uc2 Given the tumult in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far declined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring the real back down. \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  said steeper losses related specifically to the real could trigger action from the bank, however.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's SulAmerica Investimentos said it sees a gradual return to normalcy following the Cyprus bailout.\par \par \uc2 "The environment of greater risk aversion from the Cypriot crisis has kept the real pressured, causing the dollar to break the BRL2.0 barrier," the firm said in a weekly outlook. "The dollar should return to trade below that level, distancing the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@dowjones.com. [ 26-03-13 1254GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130326e93q000nk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
