\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker But  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Doesn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes   \par \uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 22:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real continued to weaken against the U.S. dollar Friday, surprising investors who had expected a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRL2.0105 to the dollar on Friday, compared to BRL2.0056 the day before, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. Thursday, the real reached its lowest level since late January amid concerns with the international economy and a deteriorating outlook for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows.\par \par \uc2 "All investors were betting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the moment the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit BRL2.00 to the dollar, said Luiz Carlos Baldan, director at Brazilian brokerage Fourtrade. "\uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't act because it knows this is not a speculative move."\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Cyprus was in talks with its international creditors over a deal to rescue the country from financial collapse as details emerged ahead of a crucial parliamentary debate over a radical bank-restructuring plan that would close the country's second-biggest lender and see its big depositors lose more than a third of their savings.\par \par \uc2 According to Reginaldo Galhardo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Brazilian brokerage Treviso Corretora, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes that an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this point would likely not produce results as moves reflect concerns with the situation in Cyprus.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to keep the real in a range of BRL1.95-to-BRL2.00 to the dollar, Mr. Galhardo said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  said Friday that the international outlook remains "complex," with growth likely to stay low for some time still. In Europe, he said, the consequences of the current debt crisis will take a while to dissipate.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at any time to make ensure stability. Though the bank doesn't have a target range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is ready to act to reduce volatility, as well as to continue building up its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as the market allows.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini also said Brazil's economy shows signs of improvement, and likely grew at an annualized rate of 4% in the first quarter of this year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Luciana Magalhaes at luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com [ 22-03-13 2121GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130322e93m000rr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
