\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Weak and Investor Wonder If  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Will Act\b0\par\par\uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes   \par \uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 14:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's real opened flat against the U.S. dollar on Friday after reaching its lowest level since late January Thursday. Investors now wonder if \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will act to prevent further weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL2.0070 to the dollar Friday morning after exiting regular trading Thursday at BRL2.0056, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't acted yet because the trend reflects what is happening internationally," said Reginaldo Galhardo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Brazilian brokerage Treviso Corretora. "Probably they think an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now wouldn't change things much," he added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to keep the real in a range of BRL1.95 to BRL2.00 to the dollar, Mr. Galhardo said, adding that difficulties faced by Cyprus showed the debt crisis can still create "other victims."\par \par \uc2 Cyprus is in negotiations with a delegation of international inspectors, known as the troika, trying to set a plan for the troubled economy.\par \par \uc2 During the last three days, the Cypriot government has been trying to set another plan to raise 5.8 billion euros ($7.5 billion), in order to receive a EUR10 billion bailout package.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazilian Finance Minister Guido Mantega said Thursday in a Senate hearing that the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at an improved to support the local industry.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president, \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2 , will speak Friday at the Brazil-France Chamber of Commerce in Sao Paulo. He is expected to discuss the outlook for Brazil's growth and inflation.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's midmonth consumer price index, or IPCA-15, rose 0.49% through mid-March compared with a 0.68% in the period through mid-February, the Brazilian Geographic and Statistics Institute, or IBGE, said Friday.\par \par \uc2 In the 12-month period through mid-March, the IPCA-15 rose 6.43% versus a 6.18% advance in the same period through mid-February. It was still above the government's inflation target of 4.5%, but within a tolerance band of plus or minus two percentage points. Inflation ended 2012 at 5.84%.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, during the meeting of the monetary-policy committee of \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , policy makers removed language seen in previous statements that it would keep interest rates steady for a "sufficiently prolonged period," signaling to the market that it was ready to raise rates at any moment to tame inflation, if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Write to Luciana Magalhaes at luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com [ 22-03-13 1319GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130322e93m000ku\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
