\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Slips 1% To BRL2 To The Dollar; Weakest Since January\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 20:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real slid further on its recent path lower Thursday to end at its weakest level since late January as investors mulled an uncertain international environment and a deteriorating outlook for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows.\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRLBRL2.0056 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.9871 to the dollar Wednesday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began the session moving weaker in reaction to soft activity data in Europe and lingering doubts over whether European authorities could find an exit for a fiscal crisis in the Mediterranean nation of Cyprus. That country's parliament this week rejected a planned bailout that would be backed by taxes on bank deposit holders.\par \par \uc2 The extension of a nagging fiscal crisis in Europe and slow recovery of growth in other economies has left doubts for some analysts about whether Brazil will continue to attract investment and trade inflows.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday reported that the country saw net dollar outflows of $990 million in the first 15 days of March and $3.5 billion in the year to date.\par \par \uc2 Local authorities, meanwhile, are giving few hints of whether they may prepare to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb a weakening of the real and its potential adverse impact on inflation.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's 12-month IPCA consumer price index has run at higher than 6% in recent months, pushing the top end of the country's inflation targeting band.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a Brazilian Senate hearing Thursday, Finance Minister Guido Mantega said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at an improved level to support local industry and that the government's policy was to continue to allow the real to "float" against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in the absence of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold the real at a stronger position, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen possibly moving to raise the country's base Selic interest rate as early as its May monetary policy meeting to help discourage rising prices and attract more incoming foreign investment.\par \par \uc2 The Selic rate currently stands at a record low of 7.25%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 21-03-13 1955GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130321e93l000sr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
