\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Brazil real hits 10-month high on monetary tightening bets\b0\par\par\uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 13:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Real closes stronger than 1.95/dlr for 1st time since May\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains follow higher-than-forecast inflation data\par \par \uc2 * Analysts warn c.bank could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb big \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices; adds performance of Brazil rate futures)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, March 8 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real rallied to a 10-month high on Friday after stronger-than-forecast inflation data increased bets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tighten monetary policy, boosting the appeal of assets denominated in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real pierced 1.95 per dollar, considered by many analysts as a boundary of an informal trading band imposed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leaving investors wondering whether the bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 The real closed at 1.9455 per dollar, 0.7 percent stronger than Thursday's close. It has gained nearly 5 percent so far this year as investors have bet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will favor a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cheapen the cost of imported goods to help fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains followed data showing consumer prices jumped more than expected in February despite a government-sponsored cut in electricity rates. The inflation data added to expectations of higher interest rates in the next few months.\par \par \uc2 "With prospects of higher interest rates, the market is becoming increasingly short dollars until the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in to draw a line," said Marcos Trabbold, a trader at B&T brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's interest-rate futures also rallied after the inflation data, with the contract maturing in January 2014\par \par \uc2 jumping 17 basis points to 7.96 percent.\par \par \uc2 The domestic yield curve priced in a more than 50 percent chance of a 50-basis-point increase in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight Selic rate in April. For May, the odds of an equal sized hike reached 100 percent. The Selic currently stands at a record low of 7.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 Banks such as \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  recommended investors stay long the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , betting that further gains would be spurred by a hike in the Selic and by inflows coming from external funding sources for \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's medium-term infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 "While risks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have increased with the outperformance and the build up of speculative positions, the appreciation trend, if measured, should not raise eyebrows in the government at the current juncture," Cassiana Fernandez, an analyst at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  in Brazil, wrote in a research note.\par \par \uc2 In a sign that more investors are reviewing their estimates to price in recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, local bank \uc2 Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco\uc2  said it now expects the real to close 2013 and 2014 at 2.0 per dollar, stronger than the 2.1 per greenback previously forecast.\par \par \uc2 "Bigger concern about lingering inflation voiced by policymakers caused the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen," the bank's analysts said in a note to clients. "Comments and actions (by policymakers) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market suggest that a real around 2 per dollar, which is closer to macroeconomic fundamentals, is currently the desired level."\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Nat\u225\'00\'E1lia Cacioli and Paula Laier in Sao Paulo; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama, Nick Zieminski and Peter Galloway)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-REAL/RALLIES (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130308e938000p3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
