\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes at 10-Month High as Inflation Rises\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 21:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--Brazil's real appreciated Friday to its strongest level against the U.S. dollar since early May, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained on the sidelines, lending support to views that local authorities plan to use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help combat inflation.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL1.9477 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL1.9602 at the end of Thursday's session.\par \par \uc2 The break past BRL1.95 to the dollar marked a major psychological milestone, as many market participants had previously assumed that level to be an unofficial floor the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would enforce through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real last raised eyebrows in late January when it was allowed to appreciate beyond BRL2.0 against the dollar for the first time in several months.\par \par \uc2 "I think they're going to use the dollar to anchor inflation," said Durval Correa, head trader at Sao Paulo's Multi-Money brokerage. "The market tested, and it looks like the dollar no longer has a floor at BRL1.95."\par \par \uc2 Brazilian authorities, led by Finance Minister Guido Mantega, have often expressed a preference for a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent years to offset some of the competitive disadvantages the country's manufacturers and exporters face. But rising inflation in recent months may have forced policy makers to rearrange their priorities, some analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The official IPCA consumer price index rose to 6.31% in the 12 months through February, precariously close to the 6.5% upper limit of the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range.\par \par \uc2 As a result, economists increasingly expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its baseline Selic interest rate this year from the current, record-low 7.25% in order to rein in the inflationary pressures. Higher interest rates tend to cause the real to strengthen by making yields on Brazilian fixed-income securities more attractive to foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 In its latest monetary-policy statement, on Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  discarded language suggesting interest-rate stability, for the time, being in favor of a more vigilant tone. The bank said it will "follow the evolution of the macroeconomic environment until the next meeting, to then define the next step in monetary-policy strategy."\par \par \uc2 But a higher Selic could threaten Brazil's nascent economic recovery following two years of subpar growth. An alternative to rate increases, some analysts say, would be for authorities to allow some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation to bring down the relative cost of imported goods.\par \par \uc2 Carlos Hamilton Araujo, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic-policy director, said last month that a 10% appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , over the course of a year, would be estimated to shave 0.70 percentage point off annual inflation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 08-03-13 2024GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130308e938000qj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
