\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Stronger as Italy Tensions Ease\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2013\par 13:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Italy completes bond sale, but yields jump to highest level since October\par \par \uc2 --Real stabilized, lesser need for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister says\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real opens at BRL1.9766, stronger from Tuesday's close at BRL1.9829\par \par \uc2 By Jeff Fick\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real opened slightly stronger against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday as market tensions surrounding Italy's inconclusive election results eased and the U.S. Federal Reserve pledged to maintain its stimulus efforts.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked a stable euro, seen as a barometer for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after Italy carried out a successful bond auction. The real opened trading at BRL1.9766 to the U.S. dollar, stronger from Tuesday's closing price fix at BRL1.9829, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Global markets were attempting to bounce back from a sharp selloff to start the week, when election results in Italy raised concerns about political stability in the debt-troubled country. Without a firm ruling coalition, the prospect that the country could abandon austerity measures aimed at curtailing Italy's debt load created a fresh wave of uncertainties surrounding the euro zone's financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Moody's Investors Service said Wednesday that the election results has negative implications for Italy's sovereign credit rating and other weaker members of the single-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bloc--and also raises the risk of a renewed flare-up of the debt crisis. Tensions eased slightly after demand for Italian bonds was strong at an auction, but the country was forced to pay the highest interest rates since October to attract investors.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players in Brazil also received some direction late Tuesday from Finance Minister Guido Mantega, who said in an interview with The Wall Street Journal that the real has stabilized at a "favorable" level, lessening the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real has traded in a narrow range between BRL1.95 and BRL2.00 since the start of this year.\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate is now less volatile and at "a level that we can live with," Mr. Mantega said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Mantega and Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  have both attributed a surge in inflation partly to the real's sharp depreciation against the U.S. dollar in 2012, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled about 10% versus the greenback. Mr. Tombini has said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would move to raise interest rates, currently at a record-low 7.25%, should inflationary pressures not retreat from an upswing to start the year. Through mid-February, inflation was running at 6.2%.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., meanwhile, Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  indicated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue recent bond-buying programs also known as "quantitative easing" until the U.S. economic recovery gains traction. Mr. Bernanke, who will continue congressional testimony Wednesday, acknowledged that the increased liquidity in global markets could encourage risk-taking and someday destabilize markets or the economy.\par \par \uc2 "Keeping long-term interest rates low has helped spark a recovery in the housing market and has led to increased sales and production of automobiles and other durable goods," Mr. Bernanke said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jeff Fick at Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 27-02-13 1223GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130227e92r000og\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
