\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  President: Growth is Not A Goal For The  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy and Brian Baskin \par \uc2 832 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2013\par 23:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's priority is fighting inflation, and not spurring growth, its president said in an interview before policy makers meet to set interest rates, even as Latin American's biggest economy struggles to escape a long stretch of slow growth.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's economy expanded around 1% in 2012, down from 7.5% as recently as 2010. At the same time, annualized inflation hit 6.2% in mid-February, close to the maximum the government has said it would tolerate.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the perception of dueling policies aimed at stimulating the economy and tamping down inflation have created confusion in the market, causing the Brazilian real to gyrate from multi-month lows to highs in the space of a few months.\par \par \uc2 "Our goal is inflation, so we have to adjust and calibrate our policies to meet our goals," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  told The Wall Street Journal. "Growth is not a goal for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 While few economists expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise rates from their record low 7.25% when Mr. Tombini and other policy makers meet March 5 and 6, some say the bank could signal in its monthly policy statement that it is considering rate increases in the future if inflation remains a problem.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation in the last few months has shown more resilience than we'd like it to show," Mr. Tombini said Saturday. "We're keeping a very close eye on these developments."\par \par \uc2 The markets are likely to welcome any signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is addressing inflation, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The government has "realized that the perception about policy credibility was very low and they started making a big effort to try to solve that," said David Beker, Brazil economist at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 These concerns have led some foreign investors to prefer other emerging markets, including regional rival Mexico, complicating Brazil's efforts to raise investment ahead of the 2014 World Cup and 2016 Olympic Games. Brazilian stocks are down about 3% so far this month, and have dived 20.5% over the past 12 months, according to the MSCI Brazil index.\par \par \uc2 "This is why Brazil's underperforming," said Kathryn Rooney Vera, senior macroeconomic strategist at Bulltick Capital Markets. "Policy risk is a big deal [because of] the issue of potentially spiraling out of control inflation and the crippling effects it can have on the Brazilian story."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini, who took over the top post at \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January 2011, said inflation remained stubbornly high because of a rise in food prices last year and a sharp decline in the value of the real, which tumbled 10% against the dollar in 2012.\par \par \uc2 He said he didn't expect a repeat performance from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 "I don't see the market driving the real that way," he said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has been at the forefront of the so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war, where central banks across the globe are trying to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep their exports competitive. Brazilian Finance Minister Guido Mantega, in 2010, was one of the first to use the term, and the government has applied targeted controls to stem capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 But Mr. Tombini said Brazil has more pressing problems than fighting off large capital inflows resulting from easy monetary policies elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think this is a war for Brazil to fight at this moment," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the real trading between 2 and 2.10 to the dollar for much of the second half of 2012. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traded anywhere from around 2.14 to 1.95 per dollar since December, however, causing some investors to speculate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was using the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a monetary policy tool to help the economy recover and combat inflation. Mr. Tombini called such speculation misguided.\par \par \uc2 "None of that is the reality," he said. "[The] exchange rate is not an instrument either to combat inflation or to sustain economic growth."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to "shave off" excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, he added.\par \par \uc2 Ultralow interest rates in the developed world and asset purchase programs by some major central banks, including the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , have resulted in a flood of liquidity in global financial markets--driving large capital flows into higher-yielding markets like Brazil's.\par \par \uc2 Despite such efforts, "slow [global] growth will remain with us for a while," Mr. Tombini said, adding however that he sees a lower risk of a shock to the world economy.\par \par \uc2 Policy makers across the globe, however, will have to ensure that unwinding such easy monetary policies and withdrawing excess liquidity is a smooth process.\par \par \uc2 "Going forward the concern will be how the world will exit this...new normal," he said.\par \par \uc2 --Matthew Cowley contributed to this article. [ 02-24-13 1804ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020130224e92o0002a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
