\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real weaker on cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , euro-worries weigh\b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2013\par 00:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazilian real closes down 0.05 pct, after cenbank move\par \par \uc2 * Brazilian Cenbank gives nod to stronger real\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso down 0.05 pct, investors eye global woes\par \par \uc2 By Alexandra Alper and Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Feb 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cooled on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the real's rally, while other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly flat on renewed concerns about the Euro-zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 The real eased 0.05 percent to close at 1.9715 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to halt the rapid rise of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- which has gained about 8 percent since November.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came despite comments by a number of policymakers, including Finance Minister Guido Mantega, suggesting the government was ready to accept a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cheapen the price of imported goods and put a lid on inflation.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Reuters on Thursday night, Mantega said the real, which last week gained past the level of 2 per dollar for the first time in seven months, "has found a reasonable floating band."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move followed a week of intense volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as investors scrambled to figure out how policymakers were adjusting Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 "While investors may be skeptical about Brazil's intentions near-term, a solid and ongoing commitment to a stable real, instead of a weaker real, may end up marking its return to being a favored emerging market trade," \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 's analysts said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The real is now likely to enter the traditional Carnival lull that will halt Brazilian markets for most of next week.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso cooled 0.05 percent to 12.727 per dollar, as renewed euro-zone concerns and upcoming U.S. spending cuts weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Latin America's no. 2 economy.\par \par \uc2 The peso has gained more than 1 percent since the close of 2012, but has been slowly pulling off a ten-month high reached on Jan. 17.\par \par \uc2 Investors "are waiting for any pretext to get some air," said Jorge Gordillo, an analyst at CI Banco in Mexico city, who said European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2 's comments on Thursday were still weighing on the peso.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Draghi said the exchange rate is important for growth and price stability, which investors perceived as a sign the bank is concerned with the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent advance and potentially could act to stem its strength.\par \par \uc2 Gordillo predicted that the peso would fall to around 12.90 to 13 pesos per dollar, as the deadline for automatic spending cuts in the United States - March 1 -- draws near.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of us analysts are saying that the peso is at its last phase of strength," he said.\par \par \uc2 PRICES 22:30\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      daily   YTD %\par                                  %  change\par              