\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes Moderately Weaker amid Global Selloff\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2013\par 20:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--Brazil's real closed moderately weaker against the dollar Monday amid broad losses in global stocks and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though investors found little relevant news for the local market.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL1.9918 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL1.9862 shortly after the open and BRL1.9865 at Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average, which Brazilian assets sometimes track, was recently down 0.9%; the euro weakened against the dollar and Brazil's Ibovespa stock index hovered 1.5% lower with less than an hour of trading left in the session.\par \par \uc2 Reginaldo Galhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sao Paulo's Treviso brokerage, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was mainly following international markets Monday.\par \par \uc2 With high inflation fueling speculation that Brazilian authorities--who wield heavy influence upon the real--might allow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen beyond current levels, "the market is cautious," Mr. Galhardo said.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Guido Mantega last week suggested investors shouldn't expect the real to strengthen suddenly against the dollar, saying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't a tool for controlling inflation. The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for its part, carried out a number of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market that effectively induced the real to strengthen beyond the BRL2.0 threshold for the first time since July.\par \par \uc2 "We've got our friend Mantega saying one thing and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying another," Mr. Galhardo said. "There aren't clear signals about whether the real will be an instrument to control inflation or if capital inflows will pick up."\par \par \uc2 Prices for some of Brazil's key commodity exports such as iron ore, sugar and coffee stood lower in 2012 than in previous years. At the same time, financial investments slipped amid a sharp slowdown in the local economy and occasional, heavy-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Brazilian authorities.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  received a net inflow of $16.75 billion in 2012, down from $65.28 billion the previous year.\par \par \uc2 In the first four weeks of January, a net $2.69 billion left the country, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 04-02-13 1902GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130204e924000xa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
