\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens Early on Local Data, Caution Abroad\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2013\par 13:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real weakened slightly in early trading Friday in reaction to flat local industrial output data and caution ahead of awaited indicators abroad.\par \par \uc2 As of 6:50 a.m. ET, the real traded at BRL1.9890 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.9887 to the dollar Thursday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the real trader weaker, but still within a tight range, after the country's IBGE statistics institute confirmed disappointing industrial production figures for December.\par \par \uc2 Output remained flat in the month and was down 3.6% on a year on year comparison. For all of 2012, Brazil's industrial production was down by 2.7%.\par \par \uc2 Investors remain cautious, meanwhile, ahead of release of job figures in the U.S., where analysts seek to discern whether the economy could continue on an unexpectedly weaker path revealed by disappointing growth data earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Locally, meanwhile, players in Brazil have been attentive to the latest signals from the government on whether it could allow strengthening of the real to improve inflation or hold it steady to boost exports and growth.\par \par \uc2 "Investors still don't know where to place bets in relation to exchange and monetary policy because of the recent conflict between the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the first favors growth and the latter is clearly concerned with inflation," noted Jefferson Rugik at the Correparti brokerage in Curitiba.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  earlier this week sent signals that the government meant to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady, but that was immediately followed by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that strengthened the real.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its recent policy notes hinted it may take a stronger stance against inflation this year, which has hovered recently around 6%. The government has set the centerpoint of its inflation targeting system for 2014 at 4.5%.\par \par \uc2 Also on the radar Friday will be Brazilian foreign trade data, as analysts look for signs of an improving trade balance. The country is expected to post a January trade deficit of around $3.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 01-02-13 1210GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130201e921000rj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
