\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Ends Stronger in Reaction to Data, Inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2013\par 20:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real gained ground to end slightly stronger Friday amid market reactions to data and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows during the session.\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRL1.9865 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.9887 to the dollar Thursday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began the session weakening amid uncertainties generated by disappointing local industrial production figures, but began to turn around later in the day as improving data in the U.S. brought encouragement.\par \par \uc2 Investors found some improvements in U.S. January jobs data that showed 157,000 posts created in the month. And both overseas and local markets got particular traction after the U.S. Purchasing Manager's Index Friday came in at its highest level in nine months at 55.8.\par \par \uc2 The data brought an especially positive impact on commodities sector assets, where Brazil is a major player.\par \par \uc2 Still, analysts cautioned that the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to remain range bound ahead, and could even weaken amid continued doubts about the prospects for inflows.\par \par \uc2 "Nothing indicates that there will be improvements in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows," said Sidnei Nehme at the NGO brokerage in Sao Paulo. "The country has lost attractiveness and there are few options for gains to stimulate foreign investors to bring funds, given that many other emerging markets look more attractive at the moment."\par \par \uc2 Still, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been seen caught between conflicting demands of the government to control local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation and also limit the impact of depreciation on inflation.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's 12-month IPCA consumer price index has remained at around 6%, despite an annual government target at 4.5%.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the country continues to suffer from a weakened foreign trade balance.\par \par \uc2 The trade ministry Friday reported the country posted a $4 billion deficit in January, the worst result on record for the month.\par \par \uc2 Given those factors, analysts expect investors could see more volatility ahead and frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid efforts to hold \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a desired narrow range.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 01-02-13 1915GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130201e9210011u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
