\par\par \b \uc2 Investors wonder who's in charge of Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy\b0\par\par\uc2 1,036 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2013\par 18:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Investors see tension between Mantega, Tombini over \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen winning case for stronger real\par \par \uc2 * Real could gain to 1.95/dlr without cenbank resistance\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Feb 1 (Reuters) - When \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to halt a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sell-off triggered by comments from Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2 , many investors wondered who is really in charge of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 It was the second time in about two months that Mantega and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  appeared to clash publicly over the appropriate level for the real - a debate that has been growing as Brazil's economic recovery has faltered and inflation has stayed above target.\par \par \uc2 Both episodes, if not evidence of conflict among Brazilian policymakers, are seen at the least as being an example of the sort of seemingly contradictory policy action that has worried investors and put a chill on Brazil's business climate.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, just one day after the real had gained past 2 per dollar for the first time in seven months, Mantega warned the government was ready to correct any "excess" in the exchange rate and that a "speculative appreciation" of the real would not be tolerated.\par \par \uc2 His comments brought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to the 2-per-dollar mark, but the change was erased minutes later when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it was rolling over $1.2 billion in dollar repurchase agreements that would expire two days later.\par \par \uc2 When the real traded at around 2.10 per dollar on Nov. 23, Mantega told a crowd of business leaders in Sao Paulo that the exchange rate was at a "reasonable though not totally satisfactory level" to support industry. He added that a real weaker than 2 per dollar "was here to stay".\par \par \uc2 In moves similar to this week's action, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Mantega's comments only to be rescued minutes later by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are seen by analysts as a sign of growing inflation concerns.\par \par \uc2 "Uncertainty rules now," Ilan Solot, a London-based emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 , said of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Like many analysts, Solot said it is tough to say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was deliberately offsetting Mantega's comments or if the timing of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a mere coincidence.\par \par \uc2 Solot said, though, that it appears that Tombini is taking the reins of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy with the blessing of President Dilma Rousseff, herself a trained economist who likes to have a say in key economic decisions.\par \par \uc2 "My interpretation is that there are two different lines of economic thinking (in the government). And the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking is gaining precedence over the finance ministry's thinking," he said.\par \par \uc2 In Brasilia, a finance ministry source said there was no conflict between Mantega's Wednesday speech and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action. "There was no contradiction. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  just did a (dollar line) rollover."\par \par \uc2 Citi strategists Kenneth Lam and Douglas Comin disagree.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not necessarily see eye to eye on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," they wrote in a research note. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has won the battle of the day in convincing the government to let the real appreciate to ease inflation."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 IMPROVING COORDINATION?\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry had a long history of disagreement over economic themes such as the right level for interest rates and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the eight years of President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's government.\par \par \uc2 While Mantega was a voice in the chorus of discontent with Brazil's double-digit interest rates, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , led by its former president \uc2 Henrique Meirelles\uc2 , carried out an orthodox policy of high interest rates and a relatively free-floating exchange rate to keep inflation at bay.\par \par \uc2 Under Rousseff and Tombini, however, the bank lowered the base Selic rate to a record low of 7.25 percent while allowing the real to devalue by nearly 30 percent in the period between July 2011 and last November. Both actions were part of a coordinated government action to boost economic activity.\par \par \uc2 But a persistent rise in inflation, combined with a still anemic economic recovery, seems to have magnified lingering tensions between the two institutions, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now pushing for a stronger real.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, the finance ministry has also been unwinding some of the measures taken early last year to curb dollar inflows, helping the real gain about 7 percent in value since the end of November.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Mantega stressed that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains do not mean the government is changing its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy nor was it trying to use the exchange rate to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 Instead, according to another source at the finance ministry, a stronger real is part of a strategy to cheapen imported capital goods and boost much-needed investment in industry - an explanation that can certainly be more easily digested by the exporters Mantega had pledged to protect with a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Market analysts, however, are not totally convinced.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help as a cushion against inflation," said Bruno Eiras Martins, a trader at \uc2 Banco Daycoval\uc2  in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "Some are saying that a stronger real is an instrument to boost imports of capital goods and investment, but I'm not sure about that. I believe that, given rising inflation concerns, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has adjusted its strategy."\par \par \uc2 While economists agree that a moderate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation would not make a substantial dent on inflation, the fact that the real pierced the mark of 2 per dollar earlier this week should at least help anchor inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 For now, most analysts agree, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should offer no resistance to a real as strong as 1.95 per dollar, as long as the appreciation is gradual.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Alonso Soto in Brasilia; Editing by Brian Winter; and Peter Galloway)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /POLICY | ABN | D | M | NAT | E | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130201e921001c7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
