\par\par \b \uc2 South Korea's Won Weakens on Finance Ministry Comments\b0\par\par\uc2 By Georgia Wells   \par \uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2013\par 20:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 South Korea's won resumed its two-week march lower Wednesday after a finance-ministry official outlined measures the government may take to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday in Seoul, Deputy Finance Minister Choi Jong-ku said taxes on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading and bonds should be considered to help limit speculative capital inflows. Among a series of other measures, he also said state firms should refrain from overseas borrowing.\par \par \uc2 The proposal highlights concern among Asian authorities over the continued low interest rates in the U.S., Europe and Japan that are driving capital flows to emerging markets and tipping off a renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war from government officials. For emerging-market officials, this means adjusting to the relative strength of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a decline in export competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 "This is a protracted effort by the government to talk down the won," said Ilan Solot, an emerging-markets strategist based in London at investment bank \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We don't know exactly what measures they're going to take, but they definitely have the credibility," Mr. Solot said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to KRW1086.2, from KRW1083.2 late Tuesday, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real traded slightly lower as markets digested an announcement of new dollar credit lines along with comments from Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The new credit lines, where \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer up to $1.273 billion, come as weaker-than-expected dollar inflows boosted demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It's a liquidity measure that's very much within the realm of the [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ]. It's not one of the tools they use to impact the [\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] rate," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, strategist at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2  in Stamford, Conn.\par \par \uc2 Comments from Mr. Mantega overshadowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures as he suggested the government wouldn't use the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to control inflation and that a weaker real should help \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's competitiveness. Last year, authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the real weaken nearly 10% versus the dollar, and this has allowed local industry to become more competitive, he said. His comments caused some confusion amongst traders, particularly since just on Monday the real broke through the psychologically important level of BRL2.00 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Amidst the confusion, the real weakened 0.1% versus the dollar, to BRL1.9884, from BRL1.9862 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "The reaction in the market...reflects the fact that the market is tired from so much noise and communication from a government that has too many objectives running at the same time with very few effective policy tools," Ms. Cattan-Naslausky added.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Mexican peso weakened following the first quarterly decline in U.S. economic growth since 2009.\par \par \uc2 U.S. gross domestic product declined at an annual rate of 0.1% between October and December, the Commerce Department said Wednesday. Mexico's main trade partner is the U.S., which leaves the country vulnerable to any weakness in the economic outlook of its neighbor to the north.\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the peso fell 0.25%, to MXN12.7485, from MXN12.7180 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Investors' attention has now turned to the Federal Open Market Committee's January policy statement due later in the day. The last time \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  policy meeting minutes were released, emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  broadly declined on signs that some Fed officials had wanted to bring the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stimulus program to a close.\par \par \uc2 --Gerald Jeffris contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Georgia Wells at georgia.wells@dowjones.com [ 30-01-13 1901GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130130e91u0010m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
