\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real, Chile peso drop on verbal  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2013\par 21:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile finance ministry, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to discuss peso strength\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't roll over dollar auctions with repo agreement -Estado\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real drops 0.5 percent; Mexican peso drops 0.3 percent\par \par \uc2 By Danielle Fonseca and Moises Avila\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Jan 8 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real dropped on Tuesday on signs that the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gain much further, while the Chilean peso weakened after that country's finance minister expressed concern about the impact of a strong exchange rate on exports.\par \par \uc2 Most Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also fell as investors took a weak Wall Street session as a cue to pocket part of a recent rally, driving the Mexican peso 0.25 percent lower.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real led losses in the region, falling 0.4 percent to 2.0373 per dollar, after local news agency Estado quoted an anonymous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source as saying that, at current exchange rates, the bank would not roll over the dollars it had sold with repurchase agreements late last year.\par \par \uc2 "That could be an indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want the real too close to two per dollar," said a trader at a large Brazilian bank.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman said the bank would not comment on a story based on an anonymous source.\par \par \uc2 Those dollar auctions were part of Brazil's strategy to provide liquidity to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at the end of the year, when greenbacks are usually more scarce as Brazilians vacation abroad and foreign companies remit profits to their headquarters.\par \par \uc2 Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was designed to strengthen the real and avoid additional inflation pressures, analysts believe policymakers also do not want the real to gain past two per dollar, which could hurt exporters.\par \par \uc2 In Chile, the peso erased early gains to close 0.21 percent weaker at 472.20 per dollar after Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may come up with "coordinated action" to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from gaining further.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso has rallied more than 1 percent in the first few days of 2013, on top of gains of nearly 8.5 percent in 2012.\par \par \uc2 "The peso started the day stronger as foreign banks sold dollars," said Eugenio Cortes, head of forward contracts at EuroAmerica. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pierced the level of 470 per dollar when investors started buying dollars again and the finance minister came with his "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.\par \par \uc2 Local analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be compelled to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso strengthens past 467 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2010 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          Daily  YTD pct\par                                    pct   change\par             