\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Stronger, Market Expects Less  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2013\par 13:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Real trading at BRL2.0214 from BRL2.0289 at Monday's close\par \par \uc2 --Market sees change in government policy to permit stronger real\par \par \uc2 --Investors ready to test \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level\par \par \uc2 By Jeffrey T. Lewis\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real opened stronger against the dollar Tuesday as the market adjusts to a perceived change in government policy, signalled by the country's finance minister, that will mean less support for a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL2.0214 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, from BRL2.0289 at the close Monday.\par \par \uc2 The government spent most of last year working to weaken the real versus the dollar to try to make Brazilian exports more competitive in world markets.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's government plans to ease back on policies to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and lower interest rates in 2013 as economic growth starts to recover after two years in the doldrums, Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  said in an interview with Dow Jones published Friday.\par \par \uc2 The government is now looking to use the exchange rate as a tool to help control inflation, said Reginaldo Galhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at the Treviso brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "The market is reading between the lines and sees a moment for the real to strengthen, at least to the point the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides it's at a good level," Mr. Galhardo said.\par \par \uc2 It remains to be seen what level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will choose to defend. During much of the second half of 2012 the market assumed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't want the real to strengthen past BRL2.0 to the dollar, and the bank stepped in and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on more than one occasion when the real moved close to that level.\par \par \uc2 The bank will probably continue to defend that level, though it might eventually permit a slightly stronger real to help keep inflation under control, Mr. Galhardo said.\par \par \uc2 Investors are probably going to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming days to try to establish where it will step in, he added.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jeffrey T. Lewis at jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com [ 08-01-13 1211GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130108e918000nc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
