\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Brazil Dollar Outflows Rise To $7.07 Billion For Dec. 1-21\b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2012\par 15:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 27 Dec 2012 09:37 EDT *DJ  Brazil Dec. 1-21 Dollar Outflows Reverse Hefty Nov. Inflows\par \par \uc2 27 Dec 2012 09:38 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  Dollar Outflows Have Meant \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 27 Dec 2012 09:40 EDT *DJ  December Could Mark Biggest Brazil Dollar Outflows Of 2012\par \par \uc2 27 Dec 2012 10:09 EDT DJ  Brazil Dollar Outflows Rise to $7.07 Billion in Dec 1-21 Period\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Pressured by heavy imports and profit and dividend remittances by multinational companies, Brazil showed net U.S. dollar outflows of $7.07 billion during the period Dec. 1 through 21, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Brazil\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The figure marked a reversal following net November inflows of $4.88 billion. If the trend continues through the end of the month, December will mark the biggest month of net outflows of the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2012.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows flipped from net positive to net negative in just one month in large part because of heavy imports. Imports typically rise during the Christmas shopping season as Brazilians snap up imported consumer goods and even some perishables. For the three-week period ended Dec. 21, net trade outflows were $4.87 billion.\par \par \uc2 But Brazil also saw net outflows on the investment side for the period totaling $2.2 billion. Foreign-investor interest in Brazil has waned for a number of reasons. One is increased volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate in recent months. Another is a rise in government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. A third reason is lower Brazilian interest rates, making fixed-income investments in Brazil less attractive. Brazil's benchmark interest rate now stands at 7.25%, down from its 2012 peak of 12.5%.\par \par \uc2 December's net dollar outflows have brought a consistent pattern of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in efforts to avoid an abrupt depreciation of the Brazilian real against the U.S. dollar. Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  six times in the market, using various auction mechanisms to increase the availability of dollars or dollar-hedging opportunities for investors.\par \par \uc2 December also typically sees an increase in demand for dollars from the Brazilian subsidiaries of multinational companies as they remit profits and dividends to overseas parents before the end of the calendar year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tom Murphy at tom.murphy@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 27, 2012 10:09 ET (15:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121227e8cr002wy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
