\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Weakens, May Prompt More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2012\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 10:00 EST - Selling pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real reverses earlier gains, prompting speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step back into the market offering greenbacks. BRL breaks above BRL2.050 per dollar, having opened stronger at BRL2.0415 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered dollar credit lines. Still slightly stronger than late Wednesday level of BRL2.0536. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:52 EST - Retail sales fell 2.5% and foot traffic dropped 3.3% in the week leading up to Christmas compared with a year ago, in the latest sign that shopping was tepid this holiday season, ShopperTrak says. Retailers shouldn't expect much of a post-Christmas boost, either. Last year, Dec 26 fell on a Monday, with many people having the day off. This year it was a Wednesday, when many were back at work. (karen.talley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:44 EST - Some investors emerge to scoop up cheapened Treasurys again, a recurring theme the past 2 months amid fiscal-cliff uncertainty. And while the top-of-the-hour economic data could give reason to trade, it might take a backseat as DC remains front-and-center. The 10-year note is now flat after earlier declines, pushing the yield back down to 1.76%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:43 EST - BOJ's stepped-up rhetoric this week to weaken the yen has encouraged investors to borrow JPY at near zero interest rate and buy higher-yielding assets elsewhere. Andrew Brenner, head of international fixed income at National Alliance Securities, points to the rallying euro/yen, which earlier rose above Y114 for the first time since Aug 2011, as "a bullish indicator for global asset prices." Brenner says he won't be surprised to see the euro rise to $1.40 vs the US dollar as the US "clearly struggles with fiscal cliff and debt ceiling." He warns downgrades of US debt are coming. Still, the dollar actually rallied in 2011 when S&P stripped the US of its triple-A rating. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:39 EST - Peru's motor vehicle loans are soaring alongside the economic boom, the nation's banking association said. Vehicle loans rose to $681M in November, a rise of more than 27% from the same month a year earlier. "The loans are expanding in line with the solidness seen in private sector consumption," the association said. Some economists are forecasting growth of more than 7.0% in Peru's economy next year. (robert.kozak@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:34 EST - \uc2 JMP Securities\uc2  notes a decent balance sheet was among investors' main reasons for overlooking other fundamental headwinds at Marvell (MRVL). But Wednesday's $1.17B patent-infringement award against the company "suddenly and significantly calls into question how much of a valuation safety net is in place for the stock." A defiant MRVL notes it hadn't carved out any liability to cover the hefty payment as of Oct. 27, suggesting management hadn't expected such a wallop to its books. After sliding 10% yesterday on the verdict, it's off another 4.8% as trading gets underway today and nearly breaks $7 for the first time since March 2009. (andrew.fitzgerald@dowjones.com; @drewfitzgerald)\par \par \uc2 9:28 EST - News that unions at the world's largest copper mine have rejected a wage offer has injected excitement into a sleepy week for metals. But does it matter? In the short term, no. Talks between workers and Escondida mine operator \uc2 BHP Billiton\uc2  (BHP) were early. It's technically illegal to go on strike before the contract expires more than six months from now. Secondly, copper stockpiles are ample. They're near a record in China and the LME's pile is up one-third in December. Long-term, a Chilean strike would upset the market and quickly end predictions for a 2013 surplus. That said, take this week's low-volume moves with a grain of salt. Comex copper is up 0.2%. (matt.day@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:27 EST - MKM Partners is girding from more sales-data disappointment from Target (TGT) and \uc2 Kohl's\uc2  (KSS) when they release December results next Thursday. It cuts its same-store-sales growth view on KSS to 1-3% from 3-5% while the TGT estimate goes to flat to up 2%, down 1 percentage point. Both logged surprise SSS declines for November, so investor sentiment isn't exactly forgiving on either company. And with TGT's \uc2 Neiman Marcus\uc2  partnership being a dud coupled with things like fiscal-cliff worries and warm weather, MKM isn't upbeat. But it does boost its sales target 1 point on \uc2 TJX\uc2 , now saying that retailer will post 1-3% growth. However, the new view isn't terribly upbeat either, considering November's 3% SSS increase was \uc2 TJX\uc2 's weakest showing in at least a year. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:26 EST - About 44.4% portion of individual stock investors feeling bullish about the stock market, according to the latest weekly survey from the \uc2 American Association of Individual Investors\uc2 . That's the ninth-highest reading this year, suggesting the fiscal cliff isn't killing average investors' optimism after all. The latest reading is down from the prior week's 46.4%, to snap a six-week streak of gains, but it looks pretty upbeat compared with a recent low of 28.8% in mid-November. Meanwhile, the S&P 500 down 1.7% the past week. (matthew.jarzemsky@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:21 EST - TD points out in a report that the USD index is barely correlated at all with the S&P 500 from a short-term point of view. However, USD/CAD's correlation with the S&P 500 remains close to -0.84 over a 30-day moving average (and the Dow Jones Industrial Index at -0.86), much stronger than its ties with commodities. USD/CAD's ties to light crude is at -0.43 and the CRB Commodity Index (+0.25). "Risk appetite is the most important short-term market variable for the CAD at the moment," TD says. USD/CAD at 0.9918, down 0.24%, according to CQG. (david.george-cosh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:09 EST - Amid its 2013 outlook on the US insurance sector, \uc2 Stifel Nicolaus\uc2  adds Hartford (HIG) and Brown & Brown (BRO) while removing \uc2 AON\uc2  as "in general, commercial-lines rate increases should modestly accelerate" the next year or 2. On the personal side, "we prefer insurers with little, or at least well-diversified and heavily reinsured, homeowners exposure." But the investment bank does "like a few recently-struggling insurers to whom rising rates should make a bigger difference." As for HIG, which has jumped 40% the past 5 months, Stifel raises its price target to $28 from $25 amid the company's continued sharp trading discount to book value amid its restructuring. Shares of all three are inactive premarket. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:54 EST - There was little reaction to US employment data, which showed jobless claims dropping 12K to 350K last week, partially because weekly data tends to become cloudy during the holidays. With Japan's newly elected government keeping yen shorts in a state of happy delirium by talking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower, consumer confidence and new home sales data should have little effect as well -- barring any major surprises. Look for data to figure more prominently on traders radar after the New Year, when people start looking for reasons to take profits on their yen shorts. JPY recently at 85.92. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Bradley Davis, 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Shipman\f28 \uc2 \f2 , 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 12-27-12 1000ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020121227e8cr00056\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
