\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken; Mexico peso slumps\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2012\par 15:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real down 0.52 pct despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Mexico's peso slips 1.43 pct, Chile's peso off 0.67 pct\par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, updates prices, changes dateline, previous SAO PAULO)\par \par \uc2 By Jean Arce\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Dec 21 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso tumbled by the most in five months on Friday after U.S. budget negotiations stalled and Brazil's real weakened despite efforts by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real shed 0.52 percent to 2.0732 per dollar, while Mexico's peso tumbled 1.43 percent to 12.9444 per dollar. The peso hit its weakest level since early December and headed for its worst one-day loss since late July.\par \par \uc2 Markets fell on Thursday after a budget plan proposed by a Republican leader failed to win support from his own party, raising the chances that austerity measures kick in next year.\par \par \uc2 U.S. lawmakers are struggling to come up with a deal to avert $600 billion worth of tax increases and spending cuts, a combination that could push the world's largest economy back into recession next year.\par \par \uc2 "The risk is rising that (talks) are going to drag into next year," said Delia Paredes, an analyst at Mexico's Banorte-IXE.\par \par \uc2 A U.S. economic downturn could hit Mexico the hardest among Latin American countries, since it sends nearly 80 percent of its exports to its northern neighbor.\par \par \uc2 Bets on a deal by U.S. lawmakers before the end of the year had spurred gains in riskier assets, such as Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Mexico's peso hit a two-month high last week.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice earlier in the day, selling up to $4 billion in two auctions with repurchase agreements. The auctions were designed to increase the supply of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  before year-end, but traders and analysts said they aim at curbing excessive losses in the Brazilian real.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said after the market close that it will sell up to $2 billion on the spot market on Dec. 26 with a repurchase agreement.\par \par \uc2 "After all the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has done, I think it wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate below 2.1 per U.S. dollar. It can even strengthen past 2.05 per dollar," said Reginaldo Siaca, manager at Advanced brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso shed 0.67 percent to 478 per dollar to close at its weakest in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2040 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                        daily %  year-to\par                                 change   date %\par                        Latest            change\par Brazil real              2.0732    -0.52     -9.9\par                                         \par Mexico peso             12.9444    -1.43      7.9\par                                         \par Argentina peso*          6.5900     0.61   -28.22\par                                         \par Chile peso             478.0000    -0.67     8.64\par                                         \par Colombia peso        1,775.4500     0.71     9.18\par                                         \p