\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Stronger as  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  Continues\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2012\par 20:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells dollar credit lines, plans Friday auction\par \par \uc2 --Pressure on real should ease as multinational companies close books\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real exits active trading at BRL2.0597 to the U.S. dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeff Fick \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO DE JANEIRO--Brazil's real closed stronger against the U.S. dollar Thursday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued its recent string of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but selling pressure is expected to ease as multinational companies close out year-end business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0597 to the U.S. dollar, according to Tullet Prebon via FactSet. That was stronger from Wednesday's close at BRL2.0683. Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  broke the BRL2.06 level late in the session, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced that it would cap the week with another auction of U.S. dollar credit lines.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar credit line sales have become the favored tool for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the past week, when the real weakened sharply amid heavy dollar outflows linked to seasonal remittances by multinational companies operating in Brazil. The real has come under pressure as the companies send profit and dividend payments back home, pushing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  toward the BRL2.10 level seen as the ceiling of the real's recent trading range.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's practically the last week of the year, and businesses are clearing out the books," said Joao Querino de Santos, a trader at Sao Paulo's J. Alves brokerage. "Next week should be very calm."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is also starting to feel the effect of recent moves to ease \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  restrictions put in place earlier this year, when the real was at its BRL1.70 peak against the dollar, Mr. Santos said. The IOF financial transactions tax on overseas loans of greater than one year was lowered, while the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also boosted the exemption level on reserve requirements for short-dollar positions held by banks to $3 billion from $1 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "When the real hit BRL2.10, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flashed the yellow light and let the market know that was the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ceiling," Mr. Santos said. The government is keen to keep the real trading between BRL2.00 and BRL2.10 to the dollar, a level seen as beneficial for local manufacturers and exporters without affecting inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Late Thursday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would sell up to $2 billion in U.S. dollars via the credit-line auction. The bank said it would sell the dollars at BRL2.0625 per dollar, Thursday's average daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate known as the Ptax. The auction will then establish the exchange rate the bank will use to buy the dollars back on March 1, 2013, although the bank said that it will pay a maximum of BRL2.08445 per dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kicked off the session with a similar auction, selling an undisclosed volume of dollars at BRL2.0791 and offering to buy them back on March 1 at BRL2.1017.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In its latest quarterly inflation report also released Thursday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  struck a neutral tone and indicated that current record-low interest rates would be maintained for a "sufficiently prolonged" period. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expects inflation to end 2012 at 5.7%, before easing back to 4.8% in 2013 and 4.9% in 2014. Economists, however, noted that the outlook remained above the government's 4.5% target, although within the tolerance band of plus or minus two percentage points.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Jeff Fick at jeff.fick@dowjones.com [ 20-12-12 1907GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121220e8ck000sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
