\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real edges up as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2012\par 13:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details on third auction, market reaction)\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real gained slightly on Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted three auctions to sell as much as $1.5 billion on the spot market with repurchase agreements, in an attempt to provide liquidity to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and boost the Brazilian real.\par \par \uc2 The auctions, announced on Monday, followed a rule change by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that made it easier for financial institutions to short sell the dollar -- another move aimed at shoring up the real.\par \par \uc2 Dollars are usually more scarce in Brazil at year-end, as Brazilians vacation abroad and foreign companies remit profits abroad to boost their bottom lines.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not say how much it sold at the end of the three auctions. But it set cutoff rates of 2.1083, 2.1163, and 2.1268 per dollar in each of the three auctions, with repurchase dates for Jan. 22, Feb. 19, and March 20.\par \par \uc2 That is the highest price the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will pay investors when buying back the dollars it is selling now.\par \par \uc2 The real last traded at 2.0939 per dollar, 0.1 percent stronger than Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-REAL/AUCTION (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121218e8ci000lw\par }\page {\