\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  pressured by US 'cliff' fears; real dips\b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2012\par 21:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil to sell more dollars with repo agreement on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more heavily if real nears 2.1/dollar level\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real falls 0.5 pct, Mexico peso steady\par \par \uc2 By Natalia Cacioli\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Dec 17 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged lower on Monday as uncertainty over crucial U.S. budget negotiations left investors unwilling to make strong bets in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso was little changed at 12.7474 per dollar, while the Chilean peso lost 0.2 percent to 474.70 per dollar despite signs of progress in U.S. budget negotiations. Investors fear that a series of automatic government spending cuts and tax hikes in the United States next year could disrupt the U.S. economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, however, seasonal dollar outflows further weighed on the real even after two \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions to sell greenbacks with repurchase agreement.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it will continue to provide liquidity to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, offering as much as $1.5 billion with repurchase agreements in three separate auctions.\par \par \uc2 Despite the actions, the real closed at 2.0957 per dollar, 0.5 percent weaker for the day and near the level of 2.1 per dollar that many traders consider the upper limit of an informal trading band imposed by the government.\par \par \uc2 The persistent pressure on the real left some traders betting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively in the market to defend the 2.1-per-dollar level.\par \par \uc2 "The market is pressured by dollar outflows this week. This is the last full week of the month, so we should see considerable outflows," said a trader with a large Brazilian bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "The real is likely to hover around 2.1 per dollar -- and that is a level that leaves traders wondering whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with swaps," the trader added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been auctioning traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps -- derivatives that emulate the sale of dollars in the futures market -- whenever it wants to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2020 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                   change   change\par                          Latest           \par Brazil real                2.0957    -0.50   -10.99\par                                           \par Mexico peso               12.7450     0.03     9.61\par                                           \par Argentina peso*            6.5000     0.46   -27.23\par                                           \par Chile peso               474.7000    -0.19     9.40\par                                           \par Colombia peso          1,796.0000     0.01     7.93\par                                           \par Peru sol                   2.5610    -0.04     5.31\par                                           \par * Argentine peso's rate between                    