\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Tombini: Global Growth Seen Low For Long Period\b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2012\par 15:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 09:24 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: Measures Abroad Cut Risks, But Won't Produce Strong Recovery\par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 09:26 EDT *DJ  Tombini: Brazil Activity Recovering Gradually, To Accelerate In 2013\par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 09:28 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: Maintenance Of Selic For Long Period To Put Inflation On Target\par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 09:29 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: Floating \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Policy Shouldn't Encourage Bets On Volatility\par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 10:05 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vigilant On Inflation\par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 10:05 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: Local Banks Healthy, Well Provisioned\par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 10:25 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: 3Q GDP Was Reasonable In International Context\par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 10:29 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: Investment To Grow In Coming Year\par \par \uc2 11 Dec 2012 10:50 EDT DJ  Brazil's Tombini: Stable Rates to Support Recovery, Low Inflation\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--The maintenance of Brazil's interest rates for a prolonged period of time will be sufficient to support a gradual recovery of the economy and keep inflation on target, \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Alexandre Tombini said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an appearance before the Brazilian Senate Economic Affairs Committee, Mr. Tombini said that despite a continued adverse outlook abroad, local economic policies currently in place would assure a rebound of investment and growth following a slowdown seen this year.\par \par \uc2 "A gradual recovery of activity in Brazil is in course that should continue in 2013," the bank president said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini noted that measures to restore confidence and growth had been taken by authorities in key economies abroad, but that these may not be sufficient to bring a strong international recovery.\par \par \uc2 "In recent months important measures were announced that reduce the chance of extreme events, but these aren't ready to bring growth," he said, adding, "The international outlook continues to be for low growth for a prolonged period."\par \par \uc2 In particular, he said that debt negotiations in Europe and the U.S. continued to bring risks to a global recovery.\par \par \uc2 He said China was preparing to reestablish a trend of expansion, but said its outlook "is for growth somewhat below recent years."\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the official said \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains "vigilant" on inflation and would continue its efforts to bring inflation toward the country's 4.5% inflation target with stable interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months has held the country's benchmark Selic interest rate record low of 7.25%.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini acknowledged that low growth of around 0.9% in the third quarter brought frustration, but said that it was in line with the performance of other economies around the globe.\par \par \uc2 "In relation to countries in the G-20, the performance of the Brazilian economy was very reasonable," he said.\par \par \uc2 He further noted that foreign direct investment remained robust and that the government in the meantime was taking measures to improve investment rates in the country.\par \par \uc2 "The diagnosis is clear, measures are being taken, and investments will take off in the coming semesters," he said.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian credit Mr. Tombini said, remained in moderate expansion, and local banks continued to be "healthy and well-provisioned" despite difficulties faced by a small group of institutions following the international credit crisis in 2008.\par \par \uc2 As part of its policy to maintain local economic stability, Mr. Tombini said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would seek to minimize volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 "Our floating exchange regime shouldn't be seen as a reason for bets on volatility," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and introduced measures to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable at a level between BRL2.05 and BRL2.10 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 11, 2012 10:50 ET (15:50 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121211e8cb0040x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
