\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil's real at 'realistic' level - Treasury\b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2012\par 14:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's stimulus measures part of "permanent" policy\par \par \uc2 * Treasury secretary indicates exchange rate at good level for economy\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes from Treasury secretary, background, byline)\par \par \uc2 By Danielle Fonseca\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Dec 11 (Reuters) - Brazil will keep stimulating its economy next year but the government believes the exchange rate has already achieved a more "realistic" level to support domestic industry, Treasury Secretary Arno Augustin said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Augustin did not specify which stimulus measures he was referring to but said the government intends to take steps to boost growth on a "permanent" basis.\par \par \uc2 President Dilma Rousseff's government has offered several tax breaks and credit incentives to spur investments and revive economic growth after a near-recession in the past year. Some of the measures, such as a tax reduction on automobiles, are due to expire at the end of this year.\par \par \uc2 "Stimulus measures will continue this and next year, this is something permanent," Augustin said at an event organized by Bloomberg in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian government has also acted in the past few months to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in an attempt to stimulate exports. But the real is at a more "realistic" level now after being excessively strong in the past, Augustin added.\par \par \uc2 The real has slipped about 10 percent since the beginning of the year after several market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a sharp cut in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's base interest rate, the Selic. It traded at 2.0755 reais per U.S. dollar on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Augustin reiterated that the government doesn't have a target for the exchange rate. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were aimed at curbing undesired volatility.\par \par \uc2 "There's no change to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy," he said. "The government aims to curb volatility in the exchange rate, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been doing great work on that."\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121211e8cb000qt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
