\par\par \b \uc2 DJ \uc2 Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Thinks Real Weakening Too Fast - Source\b0\par\par\uc2 825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2012\par 01:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes market has made an incorrect assessment of government policy, a person familiar with the policy says\par \par \uc2 --That impression in the market led to an "artificial depreciation" of the real, according to the person\par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes the real doesn't reflect economic fundamentals, the person says\par \par \uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes there has been "an artificial depreciation" of the Brazilian real as the market is working on an erroneous view of government policy, according to a person familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking.\par \par \uc2 "The market is working based on conjectures, on a belief that the government wants a weaker real," said the person, who asked not to be identified. "But there's no band. There's no roof and no floor. The market determines the exchange rate."\par \par \uc2 Current exchange rate levels versus the dollar don't reflect the fundamentals of the Brazilian economy, which, in spite of the weak performance, is "growing more" than other economies, said the person.\par \par \uc2 While debate persists about the real's fair value--it's lost around 10% against the dollar so far this year, but many economists still see it as overvalued --there is also a general perception that it has shed weight too fast against the dollar in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 There have been a series of press reports citing people close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have helped strengthen the Brazilian real over the last two days. The real traded at BRL2.0782 on Thursday afternoon, stronger than Wednesday's close of BRL2.0978, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 The signals appear to have arrested a concerted effort by some in the market to test weaker levels for the Brazilian real. The real weakened to 2.1359 in intraday trading on Nov. 30.\par \par \uc2 Last week, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched BRL2.0978 per dollar during intraday trading, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in several times to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday and Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also relaxed some restrictions on capital inflows that had been introduced earlier this year to prevent an overappreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Although officially these were more aimed at specific issues in lending markets, market players saw the move as clearly directed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "We had a problem of dollar liquidity and the government acted to solve that", said Sidnei Nehme, executive director at Brazilian brokerage NGO. Next year could be challenging for the real, as the government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , combined with historic low interest rates, has made \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  less attractive to overseas investors, Mr. Nehme said.\par \par \uc2 The efforts to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness come just as some in the rates market raised questions about monetary policy next year. There's a growing perception that the central won't raise rates in 2013 and may even start cutting them again to speed up the pace of recovery.\par \par \uc2 After timid 2.7% growth in 2011, the Brazilian economy is expected to grow just 1% or even less in 2012, despite a series of measures taken in an effort to spur growth. The government has often expressed concern that a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hinders the competitiveness of Brazilian exporters.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also constrained from cutting interest rates by above-target inflation, which is running around 5.6%. That's more than a full point higher than its 4.5% target, though still within the 6.5% upper limit of its tolerance band.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaffirmed its commitment to the interest rate stability for a "sufficiently prolonged period," in the minutes of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy meeting from Nov. 27 and 28.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the comments from the person familiar with the bank's consideration could once again raise tensions in Brasilia.\par \par \uc2 "The bigger question is whether this new 'strong BRL' policy signals, as some investors now believe, a change in the relative power between the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  over management of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," wrote Tony Volpon, a strategist at Nomura Securities in New York, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have recovered stewardship of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Still, there's no real contradiction between taking the real lower to help industry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to moderate the recent sudden depreciation, Mr. Volpon said. The process has to be managed to minimize damage to companies from a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or inflation from a weaker real.\par \par \uc2 "But there is no doubt, given the dismal growth in Brazil, that a weaker real is what the government desires," he said. "We still believe that it will settle at a 2.08-2.12 level once the high levels of noise and uncertainty around the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopefully fade."\par \par \uc2 Write to Luciana Magalhaes at luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020121207e8c70008d\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (brazil near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\int